# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# .lcl — version control ignores
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Model weights. Multi-GB and re-downloadable; GitHub rejects files
# over 100 MB outright. Models live in the user's data dir or are
# side-loaded, never in the repo.
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.onnx
*.pt
*.pth
models/*
!models/registry.json
!models/.gitkeep

# EXCEPTION: the static site's same-origin lite model. Small int4 shards
# (<100 MB each) that GitHub Pages serves so the in-browser demo runs on
# TLS-intercepting networks — nothing cross-origin to reject. This is the
# one deliberate place weights DO live in the repo.
!vendor/models/**

# OCR language data (23 MB, re-downloadable, Apache-2.0). Fetched into
# tools/tesseract/ — see that folder's README for the one-liner.
*.traineddata

# Dependencies and build output
node_modules/
dist/
build/
# ...but app/build is SOURCE (hand-written NSIS installer scripts), not build
# output. The blanket pattern above silently kept installer.nsh out of git —
# every installer fix would have vanished on a fresh clone.
!app/build/
!app/build/**
out/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Runtime state — sessions, file backups, the engine auth token,
# user settings. Private to each install and must never be committed.
data/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# The 0-byte placeholder interpreter; a real embedded runtime is
# fetched at package time, not tracked here.
python/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Logs and scratch
*.log
npm-debug.log*
*.tmp
*.local
knowledge/*
!knowledge/MANIFEST.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT SOURCE — fetched, not committed.
#
# Third-party runtimes and tool executables. Two of these exceed
# GitHub's hard 100 MB file limit, so a repo carrying them cannot be
# pushed at all; the rest is immutable, re-downloadable content with
# no business in version history. Their LICENCE files DO stay.
# Rebuild a fresh clone with:
#   node devtools/fetch-binaries.js     runtimes, tools, models
#   node devtools/fetch-knowledge.js    the shipped corpus
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
runtimes/**/*.exe
runtimes/**/*.dll
runtimes/**/*.dylib
runtimes/**/*.so
runtimes/**/*.tar.gz
tools/**/*.exe
tools/**/*.dll
tools/**/*.xml
tools/**/*.icc
tools/**/*.bin
tools/**/config8

# electron-builder installer-runtime output (asar-lock workaround bumps the dir)
devtools/dist-runtime*/

# the monotonic patch-number counter — machine-local build state, bumped every
# build; tracking it would dirty the tree on every release
devtools/build-seq.json

# RELEASE SIGNING — the PRIVATE key must NEVER enter the repo (the PUBLIC key,
# release-pubkey.pem, is committed and shipped on purpose). Belt-and-suspenders
# in case a key path is ever pointed inside the tree.
release.key
*.release.key
release-signing*
.lcl-release-signing/

# ANCIENT KNOWLEDGE working documents — session audit narrative and the
# operator's standing ground rules, written to a linked workspace root by the
# audit loop. Linking THIS repo as a workspace (the self-patch flow) must never
# put personal audit content one `git add -A` from public. The runtime appends
# these same patterns to a workspace's .gitignore (ancientKnowledge.js
# ensureIgnored) — pre-seeding them here is belt-and-suspenders, and stops that
# append from dirtying the tracked file.
ancient_knowledge.md
ancient_knowledge-*.md
ancient_knowledge.rules.md
ancient_knowledge-*.rules.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCAL / INTERNAL — not part of the public repo. Working notes, dev tooling
# state, and dev-only artifacts. The public-facing doc is README.md at the root.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
PROJECT.md
# internal build/design/planning notes
docs/

# Claude Code tooling state — worktrees, memory, session files. Never source.
.claude/

# stale root duplicates of app/main.js and app/renderer/app.js — the real files
# live under app/.
/main.js
/app.js

# local bleed-guard denylist and the dev test tied to the local notes
tests/no-bleed.js
tests/project-doc.js

# dev-only local installer screenshots — not referenced by code
devtools/installer/shots/
